sentences.t:
πῶς κ’ ἔοι εἴ τις νῶϊ θεῶν αἰειγενετάων
εὕδοντ’ ἀθρήσειε, θεοῖσι δὲ πᾶσι μετελθὼν
πεφράδοι;

sentences.l:
But if now truly you wish it, and it has become dear to you in your heart,
there is for you a chamber, which for you your dear son made,
Hephaestus, and close-fitting doors to the doorposts he fitted;

“Ready-minded now to the Danaans, Poseidon, come to the defence,
and grant them glory, for a little while at least, while still sleeps
Zeus, since around him I have covered soft slumber;

and led them Poseidon earth-shaker,
a dread sword, long-pointed, holding in his stout hand,
like lightning;

And they, shouting loudly, ran up, the sons of the Achaeans,
hoping to drag him away, and they cast thick
spear-points;

for before that had stood over him the best,
Polydamas and Aeneas and heavenly Agenor
and Sarpedon, commander of the Lycians, and Glaucus, blameless.
